Q: How to get Octopack to use custom .nuspec file? A: <p>Another way to use a custom or conditional .nuspec file with OctoPack is by adding a PropertyGroup to your .csproj file, like this:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
  &lt;RunOctoPack&gt;true&lt;/RunOctoPack&gt;
&lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
&lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
  &lt;OctoPackNuSpecFileName Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Release'"&gt;MyApp.nuspec&lt;/OctoPackNuSpecFileName&gt;
  &lt;OctoPackNuSpecFileName Condition="'$(Configuration)' != 'Release'"&gt;MyApp.Debug.nuspec&lt;/OctoPackNuSpecFileName&gt;
&lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Put the files MyApp.nuspec and MyApp.Debug.nuspec in the same directory as your .csproj file and you are good to go.</p>

Q: pointer-events:none prevents title attribute A: <p>Solution is simple. Set the pointer-event to none only on the link's active state:</p>
<pre><code>a:active {
    pointer-events: none;
}
</code></pre>
<p>This way, the toolltip is displayed, but clicking on the link does nothing. Found on <a href="https://moshfeu.github.io/show-tooltip-on-pointer-events-none-element/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://moshfeu.github.io/show-tooltip-on-pointer-events-none-element/</a></p>

Q: How to get programmatically the data usage limit set by user on Android OS configuration? A: <p>Do you want to get limit value (5GB) and warning value (2GB) in this example?</p>
<p>If so, you can get limitBytes and warningBytes by the following code, if you can use android.permission.MANAGE_NETWORK_POLICY and android.permission.READ_PHONE_STATE.<br>
However, android.permission.MANAGE_NETWORK_POLICY protectionLevel is signature.</p>
<pre><code>NetworkPolicyManager manager = (NetworkPolicyManager) getSystemService(&quot;netpolicy&quot;);
NetworkPolicy[] networkPolicies = manager.getNetworkPolicies();
Log.d(&quot;NetworkPolicy&quot;, &quot;limitBytes is &quot; + networkPolicies[0].limitBytes);
Log.d(&quot;NetworkPolicy&quot;, &quot;warningBytes is &quot; + networkPolicies[0].warningBytes);
</code></pre>
<p>(NetworkPolicyManager and NetworkPolicy classes are hidden)</p>
